research/audit/wave11-refuter-tasks/rem-integral-conventions-and-scope.md-2965-- **Where the more familiar hypotheses sit.** If $\varphi$ is continuously differentiable then $\varphi'$ is integrable automatically, and if $\varphi$ is in addition strictly monotone then the substitution can be read in either direction; neither refinement is needed above, and neither is claimed.
